Anatomy Explorer dataset (data/anatomy, and the derived meshes in data/findings)

Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
licence (CC BY-SA 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

This dataset is an adaptation of:

- Z-Anatomy - "The libre 3D atlas of anatomy", Gauthier Kervyn et al.,
  CC BY-SA 4.0. https://www.z-anatomy.com/ ,
  https://github.com/Z-Anatomy/Models-of-human-anatomy
  Z-Anatomy is itself derived from, among others:
- BodyParts3D, (c) The Database Center for Life Science (DBCLS),
  CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan. https://lifesciencedb.jp/bp3d/
- Terminologia Anatomica 2 (TA2) terms, Federative International Programme
  for Anatomical Terminology (FIPAT), as distributed with Z-Anatomy.
  https://fipat.library.dal.ca/
- definitions.json: the description texts that come with Z-Anatomy. About
  two thirds are excerpts from Wikipedia, CC BY-SA 3.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/), and end with the URL of
  the article they were taken from, where the authors are listed in the page
  history. The rest are Z-Anatomy's own short texts (CC BY-SA 4.0), some of
  them in the wording of Gray's Anatomy (1918, public domain).

Changes made: the Z-Anatomy Blender atlas was exported with tools/export_zanatomy.py
and converted by tools/build_dataset.py into GPU-ready vertex/index buffers
(vertices.bin, indices.bin), a structure hierarchy (anatomy.json), surface-sample
and depth caches (samples.npz, depth.npz). data/findings holds pathology meshes
(effusion, pneumothorax, consolidation, cardiomegaly...) deformed from those
meshes by tools/build_findings.py. Both remain under CC BY-SA 4.0.

If you share this dataset or anything derived from it, credit the sources above
and share it under the same licence. The software that reads it is MIT-licensed
(see LICENSE at the repository root); the MIT licence does not apply to this data.
